{
  "case_id": "2019-19-635",
  "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:40 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO, Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jay A. Sekulow (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No county district attorney in our nation's history has issued criminal process against a sitting President of the United States, and for good reason. The Constitution does not allow it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Yes, counsel, just a couple of questions. I'm interested in whether or not you can point us to some express language at the founding or during the ratification process that provides for this immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: We have said in the grand jury context that the public has a right to every man's evidence. Is it your position that that is, save for the President, every man's evidence, save for persons protected by privilege, and there is no privilege involved here, these are non-privileged, non-confidential papers, so is the -- the grand jury right to every man's evidence, exclusive of the President, every man except the President?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sekulow",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Supremacy Clause issue and the Article II issue here is pronounced, as this Court alluded to in Clinton against Jones, for that very reason, this idea that local prejudice would impact the President."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- how is -- how is this more burdensome, though, than what took place in Clinton versus Jones? I --I guess I'm -- I'm not sure I understand that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sekulow",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But they're his records from third-parties, Justice Gorsuch. The third-party is simply the agent custodian of the President's tax returns, on the President's statement of financial conditions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Just following up on Justice Gorsuch, just explain, if you can, the rationale for having one rule for criminal and another rule for civil."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, as the Court suggested in Clinton against Jones, state proceedings can pose a greater threat to the presidency. The 2300 prosecutors across the country necessarily place more emphasis on local interests than national ones."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: General, could you explain in more specific terms how you think this showing of special need would be carried out in district court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why are we using all that transplanted language, and why don't we get to a standard that takes care of what you're worried about, which is harassment and interference, and simply ask whether the investigation is based on credible suspicion of criminal activity and whether the subpoena is reasonably calculated to advance that investigation, a standard that looks to whether there is a good-faith basis for the state prosecutor's actions and whether the subpoena is reasonable in its scope and burdens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, secondly, I think that the special protective procedure that we are proposing here is necessary even under Your honor's general approach. After all, why would a prosecutor take the unprecedented step of issuing a subpoena to the President of the United States for personal records from a local prosecutor if he can't even show that he really needs the information that he's seeking?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to follow -- I want to follow up on Justice Thomas and Justice Kagan and really zero in on what the Article II interest is before we talk about what standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dunne",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two principles at issue in this case. One is the central role of the President in the functioning of our national government and the need to avoid interfering with the President's ability to carry out those important duties. The other principle is that under our Constitution, when a President acts as a private individual, he or she has responsibilities like every other citizen, including compliance with legal process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "articulate for me precisely what standard you think should apply in your case and in what sense is it more rigorous than that would apply in the dispute between the White House and Congress?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if you thought it was -- the President said it was impossible for him to do his job, as opposed to just being burdened? Would that -- would we have a role to limit or somehow end the grand jury process?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be your objection to a somewhat more demanding standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "DOJ",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the DOJ is proposing, as I understand it, is that in the first instance, it has to be the -- the prosecutor who goes to court, goes to federal court in this instance now, and makes an affirmative showing that there --that the standard has been met, that there's some objective basis and -- and it's -- it's -- it can't be obtained elsewhere, et cetera, et cetera. And only after such a showing has been made by the prosecutor, according to the DOJ, does the burden then shift to the President to show Article II burden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So, Mr. Dunne -- so, Mr. Dunne, am I correct in thinking then that you agree that the forum should be federal court, you agree on all the relevant considerations, the necessity of the information, that it can't be obtained elsewhere, the timing issues, all are relevant considerations; it's just who --who bears the burden?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dunne",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honors, the issue presented here today is extremely narrow but extremely important. We have a state investigation that's well founded, implicates no official conduct or executive privilege, involves a variety of third-parties, faces serious time constraints, and has been found to impose no Article II burdens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jay A. Sekulow)",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0005-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The New York district attorney, New York County district attorney, acknowledges that their subpoena implicates Article II issues and burdens. They also agree that there is harms that could arise to the presidency. We say those harms have actually existed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jay A. Sekulow)",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the irony of all of this is that the House of Representatives and the district attorney issued essentially the same subpoenas to the same custodian for the same records. The House said it wants the records so it can legislate, not for law enforcement reasons. The district attorney says he wants the same records for law enforcement reasons; he has no legislative authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-635",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a08472d716fb3b53c834e81918609ee70ab0761bbe4a0f9fb067bda6b68636ca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a08472d716fb-0005-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 1:22 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
